@LeaderJohnThune, the full SAVE America Act faces significant Byrd Rule obstacles and cannot simply be passed through reconciliation with a 50+1 majority. 

But that doesn’t mean Congress has to walk away without accomplishing something meaningful. 📜

Speaker Johnson’s Reconciliation 3.0 proposal offers a practical alternative: approximately $10 billion in federal grants to help states implement SAVE-style election safeguards. 🗳️

This isn’t the full mandatory SAVE America Act, and it isn’t a substitute for it. But it is a realistic opportunity to make progress without another potentially unsuccessful 60-vote fight. ⚖️

Leader Thune, you’ve already recognized reconciliation as a potential path forward. Now is the time to turn that opportunity into action. 

Please work with Speaker Johnson, move the funding provisions through reconciliation, and deliver meaningful election-integrity safeguards. 🇺🇸

Don’t let the perfect become the enemy of the achievable. 

The American people deserve progress, not another legislative stalemate. 

Please do your best to get it done. ⏰🚫

